Subject: [PATCH] Fail loudly when a photo cannot be read back from the disk

The s3 disk is configured with throw => false, so a failed download returns
null. file_put_contents then wrote a zero-byte file, and the real problem only
surfaced later as "getimagesize(): Error reading from ..." or an Imagick
"improper image header" error.

Reading the object into a variable first turns the silent failure into an
explicit error that names the path and the likely cause.

diff --git a/app/Jobs/ProcessPhoto.php b/app/Jobs/ProcessPhoto.php
--- a/app/Jobs/ProcessPhoto.php
+++ b/app/Jobs/ProcessPhoto.php
@@ -276,11 +276,18 @@
         Storage::disk('local')->makeDirectory($tempDir);
 
         $this->temporaryPhotoPath = Storage::disk('local')->path($tempFileRelativePath);
 
-        file_put_contents(
-            $this->temporaryPhotoPath,
-            Storage::disk('s3')->get($this->targetPath())
-        );
+        $contents = Storage::disk('s3')->get($this->targetPath());
+
+        if (! is_string($contents) || $contents === '') {
+            throw new \RuntimeException(
+                'Could not read '.$this->targetPath().' from the photo disk. '
+                .'Check that the photo storage URL is reachable from this container '
+                .'and that the object exists in the bucket.'
+            );
+        }
+
+        file_put_contents($this->temporaryPhotoPath, $contents);
 
         $this->temporaryPhotoRelativePath = $tempFileRelativePath;
     }
